The 8 Parts of SpeechNoun: Names a person, place, thing, or idea (e.g., dog, city, happiness).Pronoun: Takes the place of a noun to avoid repetition (e.g., he, she, they, it).Verb: Expresses an action, occurrence, or state of being (e.g., run, jump, is).Adjective: Modifies or describes a noun or pronoun (e.g., red, tall, happy).Adverb: Modifies a verb, adjective, or another adverb, often showing how, when, or where (e.g., quickly, very, well).Preposition: Shows the relationship between a noun/pronoun and other words, often indicating time or location (e.g., in, on, under, at).Conjunction: Connects words, phrases, or clauses together (e.g., and, but, because).

